# Mosaera configuration — copy to `.env` and edit as needed.
#   cp .env.example .env
# Everything here has a working default; real environment variables always win
# over .env. `scripts/dev-up.sh` sets the common ones for you automatically.

# --- Inference (Ollama) ---
# Default works when Ollama runs on the same host. On WSL2 with Ollama on the
# Windows host, point at the host gateway instead (dev-up.sh does this for you):
#   MOSAERA_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://<wsl-gateway-ip>:11434
#MOSAERA_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
#MOSAERA_MODEL_PM=gpt-oss:20b
#MOSAERA_MODEL_CODER=qwen3-coder:30b
#MOSAERA_MODEL_REVIEWER=gpt-oss:20b
#MOSAERA_MODEL_EMBED=nomic-embed-text

# --- BYOM: per-role model provider (#21) ---
# Each role runs on local Ollama by default. Point a role at a hosted provider
# (openai, anthropic, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) and pair it with that
# provider's model via MOSAERA_MODEL_* above. Configure keys in the dashboard
# (Settings → Model providers, admin-gated) or via the provider's native env var
# (OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, …). Hosted roles send prompts + repo
# content off-box — the default keeps everything local.
#MOSAERA_PROVIDER_PM=ollama
#MOSAERA_PROVIDER_CODER=openai
#MOSAERA_PROVIDER_REVIEWER=ollama
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Cost-modes: per-run model routing tiers (#7) ---
# Named profiles (economy/balanced/premium) each map roles to models; configured
# in the dashboard (Settings → Cost modes). A run picks a tier; this sets the
# default when none is chosen. A role a tier omits falls back to the base binding.
#MOSAERA_COST_MODE=balanced

# --- Durable memory (Postgres + pgvector) ---
# The bundled database (make up / make db-up). If host port 5432 is already
# taken, change MOSAERA_DB_PORT — it drives BOTH the published port and the URL
# below, so they stay in sync. Only set MOSAERA_DB_URL directly for an external DB.
#MOSAERA_DB_PORT=5432
#MOSAERA_DB_URL=postgresql://mosaera:mosaera@localhost:5432/mosaera
# The bundled DB publishes to LOOPBACK by default (keeps untrusted install-phase repo code
# from reaching it via the docker gateway). Override to 0.0.0.0 ONLY if your setup can't reach
# a 127.0.0.1-bound publish (e.g. WSL2 without Docker integration) and `make db-up` won't connect.
#MOSAERA_DB_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# If MOSAERA_DB_URL is set but the database is UNREACHABLE, the API refuses to start
# (ADR-0035) — degrading silently would mean no run history, parked runs that can't
# survive a restart, and user-account auth not being enforced. Set this to 1 only if you
# genuinely want a history-less API; it then boots with a loud warning.
#MOSAERA_ALLOW_DEGRADED_MEMORY=0

# --- GitLab (self-build: push a run's branch + open a merge request) ---
# Set a token (scope: api + write_repository) to enable the "Open Merge Request"
# button on a run whose source is on this GitLab. Point a run at a clone of your
# repo, approve the gates, then open an MR that runs through your pipeline.
#MOSAERA_GITLAB_URL=https://gitlab.rengifo.me
#MOSAERA_GITLAB_TOKEN=glpat-xxxxxxxx

# --- GitLab OAuth "Connect" (ADR-0104: provision a project's tokens by authorizing) ---
# Lets an admin click "Connect with GitLab" on a project's Integration settings instead
# of pasting a PAT. Register a GitLab OAuth APPLICATION on the SAME instance as
# MOSAERA_GITLAB_URL above (User/Group/Admin Settings -> Applications), with:
#   Redirect URI:  <MOSAERA_BASE_URL>/oauth/callback   (must match EXACTLY)
#   Scopes:        api
# You can set these THREE from the UI instead (Settings -> Integrations -> OAuth application);
# the secret is stored encrypted at rest (pair with MOSAERA_SECRET_KEY). These env vars are an
# OVERRIDE — set here, they win over the UI value. MOSAERA_BASE_URL is THIS instance's public
# origin (builds the exact redirect_uri). Absent everywhere => the Connect button is hidden and
# the manual token fields are used.
#MOSAERA_GITLAB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#MOSAERA_GITLAB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=gloas-xxxxxxxx
#MOSAERA_BASE_URL=https://mosaera.rengifo.me

# --- Execution sandbox ---
# docker (hardened container, default) or subprocess (weaker, no Docker needed).
#MOSAERA_SANDBOX=docker
#MOSAERA_SANDBOX_IMAGE=mosaera-sandbox:dev
#MOSAERA_SCAN_IMAGE=mosaera-scan:dev
#MOSAERA_SCAN=1
# Docker CLI is auto-detected (docker, else docker.exe on WSL). Override if needed:
#MOSAERA_DOCKER_BIN=docker
#MOSAERA_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT=300
# Dependency-install runs a target repo's build code. In the DOCKER sandbox it's
# contained (default on). In the SUBPROCESS sandbox it would run on the HOST, so
# it is DISABLED by default — set this to accept that risk on TRUSTED repos only
# (Docker remains the safe path for dependency repos).
#MOSAERA_ALLOW_SUBPROCESS_INSTALL=0

# --- Runtime ---
#MOSAERA_HOME=.mosaera
#MOSAERA_MAX_ITERATIONS=3
# Hard ceiling on max_iterations regardless of caller/UI input — clamps well under the
# LangGraph recursion_limit so a large value can't crash a run with GraphRecursionError.
#MOSAERA_MAX_ITERATIONS_CEILING=12

# No-progress circuit breaker: if a run produces the same failing validation or the
# same reviewer rejection this many times in a row, it stops and parks honestly
# ("can't complete this") instead of looping to the iteration cap. On by default.
#MOSAERA_STALL_DETECTION=1
#MOSAERA_STALL_LIMIT=3
# Plan-level breaker (#51, ADR-0056): consecutive fallback/identical plans before the run
# self-stops as an honest EARLY park (straight to the gate, before design/implement) instead
# of thrashing to the supervise give-up. Scaled by the sensitivity dial below.
#MOSAERA_PLAN_STALL_LIMIT=2

# Reliability sensitivity (#51, ADR-0056): the dial scaling every self-stop budget to model
# strength. "cautious" = a weak model self-stops early (cheap honest park); "persistent" = a
# strong model gets more rope (more delivery attempts); "balanced" = today's budgets. A strong
# cloud model wants "persistent"; a small local model wants "cautious".
#MOSAERA_RELIABILITY_SENSITIVITY=balanced

# Tester file cap (#51, ADR-0056): the most files the Proctor may touch in one authoring pass,
# bounding a red-hunt that would otherwise sprawl. Scaled by the sensitivity dial above.
#MOSAERA_TESTER_FILE_CAP=10

# Deliver-with-caveat: when a project type has no automated validator (a JS project,
# or an unrecognized repo), the delivery gate parks forever. Turn this ON to deliver
# such runs instead — the reviewer still gates acceptance — recorded honestly as
# "unverified", not "pass". OFF by default (park). Config/data (JSON/YAML/TOML) repos
# are validated by parsing and are unaffected.
#MOSAERA_DELIVER_UNVERIFIED=0

# Per-run spend ceilings. MOSAERA_RUN_MAX_* PARK for approval when crossed (raise and
# continue, or stop). MOSAERA_RUN_HARD_MAX_* are absolute backstops that CANCEL the
# run outright (not re-askable) so a non-converging run can't be funded forever. All
# off (unset) by default.
#MOSAERA_RUN_MAX_USD=
#MOSAERA_RUN_MAX_TOKENS=
#MOSAERA_RUN_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=
#MOSAERA_RUN_HARD_MAX_USD=
#MOSAERA_RUN_HARD_MAX_TOKENS=

# --- Code-quality revise loop (Phase 2) ---
# OFF by default: the per-run quality ring stays advisory-only. When on, a change
# whose code quality is below bar loops back for a TARGETED per-dimension revision
# (Style/Types/Complexity/Cleanliness) before the delivery gate. Best-effort: it
# never blocks working code — if it can't reach bar within the budget it delivers
# the improved result anyway. Python-only (ruff/mypy).
#MOSAERA_QUALITY_REVISE=0
#MOSAERA_QUALITY_MIN=80          # composite floor (0..100)
#MOSAERA_QUALITY_DIM_MIN=70      # per-dimension floor (0..100)
#MOSAERA_QUALITY_MAX_REVISES=1   # cap on quality revises (shares MAX_ITERATIONS budget)

# --- Reviewer auto-fix loop ---
# ON by default: a reviewer REQUEST_CHANGES verdict routes back to a TARGETED coder
# revise (bypassing plan/design) before the delivery gate, so the human gate is
# reserved for delivery. The correctness analogue of the always-on test self-heal;
# the no-progress breaker stops a loop that keeps drawing the same rejection. Shares
# the MAX_ITERATIONS budget. Set to 0 to keep the legacy behavior (park / re-plan).
#MOSAERA_REVIEW_FIX=1
# Sub-cap on reviewer-fix revises (mirrors the hygiene/quality sub-caps).
#MOSAERA_REVIEW_MAX_FIXES=2

# Stream each agent turn's reasoning (narration / chain-of-thought) to the run
# transcript — ON by default. One block per model turn, not a token firehose. Set to
# 0 to silence agent reasoning in the transcript (tool calls + results still show).
#MOSAERA_STREAM_REASONING=1

# --- In-loop hygiene gate (format / lint / types) ---
# ON by default: after tests pass, the run auto-formats and applies safe lint autofixes
# (deterministic, no model tokens), then loops the coder on the residual BLOCKING issues
# — mypy type errors and ruff F-class real-bug lint (undefined names, etc.). Python-only,
# best-effort (a missing tool is skipped, never blocks). MAX_FIXES sub-caps the coder loop
# within MAX_ITERATIONS so hygiene can't starve the reviewer loop. Set GATE=0 to disable.
#MOSAERA_HYGIENE_GATE=1
#MOSAERA_HYGIENE_MAX_FIXES=2

# --- API server ---
# Loopback by default. The API runs code and holds repository tokens and has no
# auth unless MOSAERA_API_TOKEN is set — the server REFUSES a public bind
# (non-loopback host) without a token. Only expose it deliberately, with a token.
#MOSAERA_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
#MOSAERA_API_PORT=8000
# Multi-user login (recommended for a team): once a database is configured
# (MOSAERA_DB_URL, above), the FIRST administrator is created by the terminal
# wizard — `uv run mosaera-setup`, run on the host (ADR-0116). There is no
# browser path to a first account: being able to run that command is itself the
# proof of control a setup token used to stand in for. Then per-user login
# (session cookie) takes over and an admin manages up to 5 accounts in
# Settings. No password ever goes in this file.
# MOSAERA_API_TOKEN below stays valid as a SERVICE token (CI, the transcript API,
# scripts) alongside user login — it grants API access but NOT admin config writes.
# Set it to 1 to mark the session cookie Secure (HTTPS-only) behind TLS; leave off
# for a plain-http loopback/LAN deploy. On a non-loopback bind it must be DECLARED —
# guard_bind refuses to start while it is unset, because the LAN-shaped default is wrong
# behind TLS and forcing Secure would break plain http (a browser will not send a Secure
# cookie over http://). An explicit 0 is a valid answer; silence is not (ADR-0126).
#MOSAERA_COOKIE_SECURE=0
# Bearer token required on every /api request when set (Authorization: Bearer …).
# Required for any non-loopback bind. Generate one, e.g.: openssl rand -hex 32
#MOSAERA_API_TOKEN=
# ADMIN token (X-Mosaera-Admin header): the second tier. The API token grants
# run/read; this grants config/secret writes (GitLab tokens, pricing). Proxy-safe
# (no IP heuristics). On a token-protected instance, config changes REQUIRE it;
# unset + loopback keeps config open for single-operator dev. Set it for any team
# deployment. Generate one, e.g.: openssl rand -hex 32
#MOSAERA_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# Headless first admin (orchestrated deploys). Interactively the terminal wizard
# creates the first account (`uv run mosaera-setup`, ADR-0116); where no human is
# at a terminal, set BOTH of these and the API seeds the admin directly at boot —
# zero open window, no browser step. Ignored once any account exists.
#MOSAERA_INITIAL_ADMIN_USER=
#MOSAERA_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Encrypt secrets AT REST (GitLab project tokens + BYOM provider API keys). OPT-IN and
# backward-compatible: unset → secrets are stored plaintext exactly as before; set to a
# Fernet key → they are envelope-encrypted (ADR-0039), migrating lazily on next write.
# STRONGLY RECOMMENDED even for a single-operator install: Mosaera runs the target repo's
# UNTRUSTED build/test code, which (during the egress-on install phase) could reach the
# durable-memory DB. With this key set, everything it could read there is ciphertext, not a
# plaintext GitLab PAT. Pair with the loopback DB bind (infra/docker/compose.yaml).
# Generate one: python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
# Losing this key means losing access to the secrets it encrypted (rotate them + clear).
# Since ADR-0126 the SETUP WIZARD mints one for every install, so a wizard-installed instance
# already has a value here and does not need this line. REQUIRED for any non-loopback bind:
# guard_bind refuses to start an exposed instance whose credentials are plaintext at rest.
#MOSAERA_SECRET_KEY=
# Extra browser origins allowed in dev (comma-separated); Vite dev is preset.
#MOSAERA_API_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# Model rates in $/1M tokens, JSON. Two forms per model:
#   [input, output]                              — no cache rates; priced as it always was
#   [input, output, cache_write, cache_read]     — Anthropic-style prompt caching
# SHADOW PRICING: give your LOCAL models a rate too. Nothing is billed — an on-box model's
# dollars are reported separately as `shadow_usd` and never enter `usd`, which is what the
# budget caps enforce — but the burn becomes VISIBLE before you ever pay for it. Worth doing
# before pointing any role at a hosted API: one measured run split 450,357 input / 11,995
# output (97.4% input), and adding a single comment line to one file cost ~43,000 tokens.
# Price a local model at the rate of the hosted model you would replace it with, so the number
# answers "what would this run have cost?".
#MOSAERA_MODEL_PRICES={"qwen3.6:35b": [3.0, 15.0], "gpt-oss:20b": [0.15, 0.60], "claude-sonnet-4-6": [3.0, 15.0, 3.75, 0.30]}

# Let the PM look things up while you're talking to him (ADR-0111). Off by default, and off is
# exactly the single model call it has always been — so turning it on is a clean before/after.
# On, a chat turn becomes a short bounded loop: Quincy can query this project's OWN records —
# what's blocked, how it tends to fail, which items took several runs, which acceptance text
# failed — instead of answering from whatever the server guessed to put in the prompt. Read-only,
# and only those records: the repository stays out of the chat.
# Costs several model calls per turn, so a local model will feel slower until the chat streams.
#MOSAERA_PM_CHAT_TOOLS=1

# --- deployment identity -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Mosaera deployment is identified by the DIRECTORY it was installed into: every compose call
# passes `--project-directory`, so this install's container, network and volume all carry that
# directory's project prefix. `make down` and the wizard's uninstall can therefore only ever touch
# THIS install — which matters on a server already running other Postgres containers.
#
# Set this only to override that derived name (two checkouts with the same directory name, or an
# install that predates directory scoping and must keep the volume it already has).
#COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=mosaera
